  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0067036_Question.png\" style=\"width: 252px; height: 120px;\" /></p><p>Using energy conservation, we get</p><p><math> <mrow> <mo>mgl cos</mo> <mi>&#952;</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>mv</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>mv</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>mgcos&#952;</mi></math></p><p>As the mass is moving in a circular motion, applying circular motion equation,&nbsp;<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>T</mtext> <mo>-</mo> <mtext>mg cos</mtext> <mi>&#952;</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mtext>mg cos</mtext> <mi>&#952;</mi> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>T</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mn>3</mn> <mtext>mg cos</mtext> <mi>&#952;</mi> </mrow> </math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Tsin&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>mg</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>Tcos&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mn>3</mn> <mtext>mg cos</mtext> <mi>&#952;</mi> <mo>sin</mo> <mi>&#952;</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mi>&#956;</mi> <mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>mg</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mn>3</mn> <mtext>mg</mtext> <msup> <mo>cos</mo> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mi>&#952;</mi> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mi>&#952;</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mn>4</mn> <msup> <mn>5</mn> <mo>&#8728;</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math></p>",
